## Why the build failed

In Jimmer 0.9.111, **KSP rejects more than one immutable model declaration per Kotlin file**. The check covers `@Entity`, `@MappedSuperclass`, `@Embeddable`, and `@Immutable` types — putting two `@Entity` interfaces in one `.kt` file fails KSP generation. It's a generator limitation of this release, not the runtime.

## How Kotlin models should be laid out

- **One Jimmer model declaration per Kotlin source file.** Two entities → two files.
- Keep model interfaces in their normal (often common) package so the generated facades are emitted there; `Book { ... }` lives in the model's package.
- Same file rule applies in both languages: use separate files in both Java and Kotlin source sets.
- Compile with KSP/APT to verify, and test a representative save when keys/ownership change — compilation doesn't prove DB constraints.

## Creating an `example.Book` draft in 0.9.111

Kotlin (both return the immutable `Book`, never a draft):
```kotlin
// generated factory in the model's package
val book = Book {
    name = "Jimmer Guide"
    price = BigDecimal("29.90")
}

// equivalent older spelling; emitted into the same file
val book2 = new(Book::class).by {
    name = "Jimmer Guide"
    price = BigDecimal("29.90")
}
```
with `org.babyfish.jimmer.kt.new`.

Java equivalents (APT-generated facades; `Immutables`/`Tables`/`TableExes`/`Fetchers` are generated per common package):
```java
Book book = Immutables.createBook(draft -> {
    draft.setName("Jimmer Guide");
    draft.setPrice(new BigDecimal("29.90"));
});

// identical $-style call
Book book2 = BookDraft.$.produce(draft -> {
    draft.setName("Jimmer Guide");
    draft.setPrice(new BigDecimal("29.90"));
});
```

## Jackson 2 module

`org.babyfish.jimmer.jackson.ImmutableModule`:
```java
ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper().registerModule(new ImmutableModule());
```
The newer suffixed modules do not exist in this release.

## Remaining work / next steps

Nothing was completed against a real project — I only answered from the provided reference. If you want this verified against the actual workspace, the next step is to split the offending `.kt` file into one entity per file, rebuild KSP, and confirm the generated `Book { ... }` factory and `ImmutableModule` class are on the 0.9.111 classpath.
